From a210c43524bf0f4eb6a96b803c2c8d1967c6f237 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ElXreno <elxreno@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:03:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: zero dumb buffers in video memory before handing
 them out

nv_drm_dumb_create() allocates scanout memory in video memory and maps
it, but never clears it, so a new dumb buffer holds whatever was in that
memory before: the firmware boot logo or frames of an earlier DRM
master.

The fbdev console makes this visible. With two displays of different
sizes, drm_fb_helper allocates the fbdev buffer for the largest mode but
draws the console only into the area of the smallest one, and the rest
of the buffer is scanned out unchanged on the larger display. A
3840x2400 laptop panel next to a 2560x1440 monitor shows sliced copies
of the BGRT logo to the right of the console after plymouth exits, on
every VT switch and at shutdown, and nothing ever draws over them.

Clear the buffer through the write-combined mapping once it is set up.
Dumb buffers in system memory have no such mapping here and are left
as they are.
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-gem-nvkms-memory.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-gem-nvkms-memory.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-gem-nvkms-memory.c
index 0785dddf..f413d663 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-gem-nvkms-memory.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-gem-nvkms-memory.c
@@ -508,6 +508,11 @@ int nv_drm_dumb_create(
         goto fail;
     }
 
+    if (nv_nvkms_memory->pWriteCombinedIORemapAddress != NULL) {
+        memset_io(nv_nvkms_memory->pWriteCombinedIORemapAddress, 0,
+                  nv_nvkms_memory->base.base.size);
+    }
+
     return nv_drm_gem_handle_create_drop_reference(file_priv,
                                                    &nv_nvkms_memory->base,
                                                    &args->handle);
-- 
2.55.0

